---
import Callout from "astro-theme-university/components/Callout.astro";
import CourseLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import SourceTable from "../../components/SourceTable.astro";
import { evidenceUrl } from "../../lib/evidence";
import { markdownTable } from "../../lib/mdtable";

// This page is the research package's claim-boundary table, parsed from the
// authoritative document at build time rather than retyped. If the document
// changes, the page changes; if the table empties, the spec test fails.
const boundaries = markdownTable("CLAIMS_AND_CAVEATS.md");
---

<CourseLayout
  title="What we do and do not claim"
  kicker="Reference"
  description="Every empirical statement on this site, paired with the overclaim it is
    routinely confused with. This page is the research package's own boundary table,
    rendered — not summarised."
>
  <p>
    A course built on twenty-one specimens and one 483-line program can say a
    lot of true things and almost no general ones. The distinction is not
    modesty, it is the subject: the two most instructive results here are a
    rewrite that looks correct and is not, and a lift that verifies and
    miscomputes. Both would have been reported as successes by anyone willing to
    describe their evidence loosely.
  </p>

  <p>
    So the left column below is what the evidence supports. The middle column is
    the sentence people write instead — deliberately included, because
    recognising your own draft in it is the point. The right column is the
    evidence and the qualification.
  </p>

  <Callout type="warning">
    <p>
      <strong>This page is generated.</strong> The {boundaries.rows.length} rows
      come from{" "}
      <a href={evidenceUrl("CLAIMS_AND_CAVEATS.md")}>CLAIMS_AND_CAVEATS.md</a> in
      the research package, parsed while the site builds. Nothing here is a
      paraphrase. Where a row's evidence link points at an artefact this site
      publishes, it is a link; where it points at something held back, the text
      stays and the link does not.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <SourceTable table={boundaries} rowHeaders={false} class="sc-wide" />

  <h2>The scope checklist</h2>
  <p>
    The same document ends with the checklist every page here was written
    against, and the one A1, A2 and the capstone are marked against:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>name the specimen and the optimisation level;</li>
    <li>identify the representation and the metric convention;</li>
    <li>link the retained evidence;</li>
    <li>state the relevant input and state assumptions;</li>
    <li>distinguish SAT, UNSAT and UNKNOWN;</li>
    <li>
      say whether an executable was actually produced, and whether it was
      validated.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Four things this site will never say</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      That the Polaris flattening rewrite worked. It produces a smaller graph
      and the wrong answer, and it is on this site as a failure.
    </li>
    <li>
      That a smaller control-flow graph is evidence of correct deobfuscation.
    </li>
    <li>
      That verifier-valid LLVM IR is evidence of a faithful lift. One retained
      lift is verifier-clean and wrong on 3,917 of 4,118 inputs.
    </li>
    <li>
      That a BinProtect protected output is a working sample. All eight tested
      outputs crashed or hung.
    </li>
  </ol>
</CourseLayout>
